    'UI_VOL_CDP_FAILOVER' => "Failover",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_MODE_REAL_TIME_SYNC' => "Real-time Backup",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_MODE_REAL_TIME_REPLICATION' => "Primary-Backup Replication",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_MODE_REAL_TIME_SYNC_AND_REPLICATION' => "Real-time Backup + Primary-Backup Replication",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_EXECUTION_MODE_DESC' => "Backup Mode Description",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_STANDBY_NOT_CONF_DESC' => "Standby Not Configured",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TAKE_TEMP_AGENT_DESC' => "Disaster Recovery Lab",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TAKEOVER_DATA_SOURCE_HOST' => "Data Source Host",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_VERIFY_TYPE' => "Verification Type",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_VERIFY_VOLUME' => "Verify Volume",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_MOUNT_VERIFY_DESC' => "Mount Verification",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_COMPLETE_MACHINE_VERIFY_DESC' => "Whole Machine Verification",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_TASK_STANDBY_TYPE_DESC' => "Mount Failover: Use the proxy client as the standby machine. You need to prepare an operating system identical to the host and install the same application software and backup plugins as on the host.<br><br>
                                            Whole Machine Failover: Use the disaster recovery lab as the standby machine. You need to configure the virtual standby machine's computing resources and network resources according to the host's resource configuration.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_STANDBY_TYPE_DESC' => "Proxy Client: Uses a proxy client as the standby, requiring pre-preparation of an identical operating system to the primary host and installation of matching application software and backup plugins.<br><br>
                                    Disaster Recovery Lab: Utilizes the disaster recovery lab as the standby, necessitating allocation of virtual standby's compute and network resources based on the primary host configuration.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_SYNCS_MODE_DESC' => "This mode comprises initial synchronization and real-time synchronization phases.<br><br>
                                        Initial Synchronization: Completely synchronizes existing original data from the selected data volume to the backup server. Upon completion, it enters the real-time synchronization phase.<br>
                                        Real-time Synchronization: Synchronizes changes in the selected data volume, occurring since initial synchronization, in real-time to the backup server, generating backup sets for recovery and failover.<br><br>
                                        Suitable for backup scenarios with high RPO requirements for data; users can restore or manually take over from any point in time within the backup set as needed.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_REPLICATION_MODE_DESC' => "Comprises initial synchronization and real-time synchronization phases, suited for migration scenarios with specific RPO/RTO requirements. Combined with livecd, it enables full machine migration.<br><br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_SYNC_AND_REAL_REPLI_MODE_DESC' => "Consists of initial synchronization and real-time synchronization phases, fitting backup scenarios with RPO and high application availability demands. Users can restore or manually take over from either the standby or any point in the backup set as necessary.<br><br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_INIT_SYSNC_DESC' => "Fully synchronize all existing original data in the selected data source host volume, along with any changes generated after initiating the job, to the standby machine.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_REAL_TIME_SYSNC_DESC' => "Real-time synchronize any changes in the selected data source host volume that occur after the initial synchronization is complete, to the standby machine.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_SYNC_OR_REAL_REPLI' => "Involves six stages: initial sync, real-time sync, failover initiation, in failover, rollback to initial sync, and rollback to real-time sync. Tailored for backup scenarios demanding high RPO and application availability but with limited standby storage. Users may also restore or manually take over from any backup set point as required.<br><br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_COPY_AND_AUTO_TAKEOVER_DESC' => "Features six stages including initial sync, real-time sync, failover start, in failover, rollback to initial sync, and rollback to real-time sync. Designed for backup scenarios with high availability requirements.<br><br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_COPY_AND_BACKUP_AUTO_TAKEOVER_DESC' => "Includes six stages: initial sync, real-time sync, failover start, in failover, rollback to initial sync, and rollback to real-time sync. Suited for scenarios with stringent RPO and high application availability needs. Users can also restore or manually take over from either the standby or backup set as necessary.<br><br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_INIT_SYNC_DESC' => "Initial Synchronization: Transfers all existing original data from the selected data volume to the backup server. Post-initial sync, it transitions to real-time sync.<br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_TIME_TAKEOVER_INIT_SYNC_DESC' => "Completely synchronize all existing original data in the selected data source host volume, as well as any changes produced after initiating the job, to the backup system.<br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_MODE_DESC' => "This mode includes the following job phases:",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REAL_TIME_NO_TAKEOVER_INIT_SYNC_DESC' => "Real-time synchronize any changes in the selected data source host volume that occur after the initial synchronization completes, to the backup system.<br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_BACKUP_REAL_TIME_SYNC' => "Real-time Backup Update: Following the completion of the initial sync, it constantly mirrors changes from the chosen source host volumes to the backup infrastructure, producing backup sets instrumental for restoration and seamless continuity management.<br>",
    'UI_PLATFORM_DES_TAKEOVER_STARTING_DESC' => "Failover Initiation: Activates the business continuity process when primary applications or networks fail, shifting data and applications to the standby.<br>",
    'UI_PLATFORM_DES_IN_TAKEOVER_DESC' => "In Failover: Post successful initiation, the standby initiates data and applications, replacing the primary to serve clients. When the primary issue is resolved, rollback can be executed.",
    'UI_PLATFORM_DES_BACK_INITIAL_SYN_DESC' => "Rollback to Initial Sync reverses the data generated during the failover back to the primary and backup server, followed by real-time sync rollback. Data generated post-rollback is also reversed, allowing for stopping the failover operation and resuming services from the primary.<br>",
    'UI_PLATFORM_DES_BACK_SYN_DESC' => "After the initial synchronization of the switch-back is completed, the changed data continues to be synchronized back to the source host. If the ['Backup Data'] option in the failover switch-back configuration is enabled, the changed data is also synchronized to the backup server. At this point, you can execute the stop-failover operation to revert the service to the source host, which will then provide services externally.<br>",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TAKEOVER_TYPE_CHANGE' => "Select Failover Type",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_MOUNT_TAKEOVER' => "Mount Failover",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_COMPLETE_MACHINE_TAKEOVER' => "Whole Machine Failover",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TEMP_USE_SCENE' => "Application Scenarios",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TEMP_USE_SCENE_DESC' => "In failover scenarios, the standby assumes the primary's applications and IP, providing services after app startup.<br><br>
                                        In verification scenarios, the standby takes over the primary's applications without its IP, requiring manual validation of data integrity.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_STANDBY_CONF' => "Failover Standby Configuration",
