    'UI_VOL_CDP_STANDBY_USE_VERIFY' => "Verify",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_DISABLED_AUTO_TAKEOVER' => "Disable Auto Failover",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TEMP_VM_NET_CONF' => "Network Configuration Information",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_TAKEOVER_IP_DRIFT_TIPS' => "Taking over will cause the host IP to drift, which may result in IP conflicts. Removing the network configuration will prevent the host IP from drifting after a successful failover.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_REAL_TIME_TAKEOVER_DESC' => "When a hardware, software application, or network failure occurs on the source host, initiate the business failover process to resume data and applications from the standby server.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_REAL_TIME_BACK_INITIAL_SYN_DESC' => "Synchronize the data taken over by the standby server and the data generated during the failover process back to the source host. If the ['Backup Data'] option in the failover switch-back configuration is enabled, it is also synchronized to the backup server, after which the task enters the real-time synchronization phase for switch-back.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_REAL_TIME_BACK_TIME_SYN_DESC' => "After the completion of the initial synchronization for switch-back, the subsequent changed data continues to be synchronized back to the source host. If the ['Backup Data'] option in the failover switch-back configuration is enabled, the changed data is also synchronized to the backup server. You can now execute the stop-failover operation to revert services to the source host, which will resume serving externally.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_REAL_TIME_INIT_SYNC_DESC' => "Completely synchronize the existing original data in the selected source host volume and any changes generated after the task starts to the backup system and the standby server.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_REAL_TIME_SYN_DESC' => "Real-time synchronize the changes generated in the selected source host volume after the initial synchronization to the backup system and the standby server.",
    'UI_VOL_CDP_REPLICATION_TAKEOVER_INITIAL_SYN_DESC' => "Synchronize the data taken over by the standby server and the data produced during the failover process back to the source host. If the ['Backup Data'] option in the failover switch-back configuration is enabled, it is also synchronized to the backup server.",
