    'UI_STRATEGY_FULL_TOOLTIPS' => "Full Backup: <br>It's the most complete type of backup, it will create a full copy of the data assets to the backup repository. ",
    'UI_STRATEGY_INCR_TOOLTIPS' => "Incremental Backup: <br>It backs up the new and changed data since the last backup (full or incremental).",
    'UI_STRATEGY_DIFF_TOOLTIPS' => "Differential Backup: <br>It backs up the new and changed data since the last full backup was created.",
    'UI_STRATEGY_PINCR_TOOLTIPS' => "Forever Incremental Backup: <br>It starts with an initial full backup and then runs incremental backups without any further full backups. In other words, it always backs up the new and changed data comparing to the previous backup.",
    'UI_STRATEGY_THREE_TOOLTIPS' => "Generally, we recommend you to perform full backups weekly or monthly and perform incremental backups on daily basis.",
    'UI_STRATEGY_LOG_TOOLTIPS' => "Archive log backup involves backing up the log data that has changed since the last backup.",
    'UI_STRATEGY_LOG_TOOLTIPS_TIDB' => "Archive log backup involves backing up the log data that has changed since the last backup, dependent on the previous log timestamp or incremental timestamp or differential timestamp or full timestamp. Log backups are subject to the configuration parameter GC Lifetime. If you wish to speed up log backups, you may modify the configuration yourself.",
