    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_MODE' => "Transfer via",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_NBD' => "LAN ",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_NBD_VMWARE' => "NBD",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_NBD_XENSERVER' => "NBD",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_NBD_SAN_XENSERVER' => "SAN+NBD",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_NBDSSL' => "Encrypted Transfer",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_NBDSSL_VMWARE' => "NBD-SSL",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SAN' => "SAN (LAN-free)",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HOT' => "HOTADD",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HOT_VMWARE' => "HOTADD",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HOT_VMWARE_TIPS' => "Windows machines are not recommended for hot-add transport mode for recovery/migration. It is suggested to use NBD transport!",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_ADAPTIVE' => "Auto",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first.<br><br>NBD-SSL: Transfer backup data over LAN and encrpt the transmission channel using SSL protocol. <br><br>HOTADD(LAN-free): Use the VMware ESXi HotAdd feature to attach the target VM disk to Vinchin backup server/proxy for direct data access.<br><br>If SAN transmission is not available, system will automatically switch to LAN transmission. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_VMWARE_SELECT_TIPS' => "NBD: Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first.<br><br>NBD-SSL: When data is transmitted over LAN, SSL is used to encrypt the transmitted data. <br><br>HOTADD: Mount the target disk to the backup server/node/proxy VM using the SCSI HotAdd feature of ESXi to achieve direct data access.<br><br>If SAN transmission is not available, system will automatically switch to NBD transmission. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_ICS_VVDK_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SELECT_NBD_TIPS' => "The network will be switched automatically. If there is a dedicated backup network, the private network transmission will be preferred, otherwise the network will be switched to the management network for transmission.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HUAWEI_KVM_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>NBD: Data to be transferred to backup storage through the API provided by the virtualization platform.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_RHV_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN:Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN(LAN-free):Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first.<br><br>ImageIO:Transferring virtual disk images and VM backups when using oVirt backup API.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HUAWEI_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first.<br><br>Encrypted Transfer: The backup data encrypted over SSL<br><br>If SAN transmission is not available, system will automatically switch to LAN transmission. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_LEIXEN_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first. <br><br>If SAN transmission is not available, system will automatically switch to LAN transmission. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_OPENSTACK_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first. <br>If SAN transport is not effective, it may cause the task to fail.<br><br>Proxy: Backup data is transmitted to the backup storage through a proxy resource pool or a single transmission proxy.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_XENSERVER_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first. <br><br>NBD:Backup data to be transferred by means of NBD to backup storage, XenServer7.3 and higher versions supported.<br><br>SAN+NBD:Backup data to be transferred by means of NBD+SAN to backup storage.<br><br>If SAN transmission is not available, system will automatically switch to LAN transmission.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_XENSERVER_SELECT_TIPS2' => "LAN: Data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>SAN (LAN-free): Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via storage area network. To transfer via SAN (LAN-free), you need to add LAN-free path from <strong>Resources</strong> > <strong>Infrastructure</strong> > <strong>LAN-free</strong> page first.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SCP_SELECT_TIPS' => "LAN: Backup data to be transferred from production storage to backup storage via LAN.<br><br>Please do not enable this option if you don't have a backup proxy deployed in your ESXi cluster.",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HOTADD' => "HotAdd Transmission ",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>Encrypted transport: SSL encryption for transmission channels in network transport mode",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_VMWARE_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "NBD transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>NBD-SSL transport: SSL encryption for transmission channels based on NBD transport<br><br>HotAdd transport: Mount target disks to backup server/agent through ESXI's SCSI HotAdd feature for direct data access",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_RHV_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>ImageIO transport: Transmit backup data to backup storage media through virtualization platform interfaces",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_HUAWEI_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>Encrypted transport: SSL encryption for transmission channels in network transport mode",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_LEIXEN_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SMARTX_SELECT_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>SAN transport (LAN-free): Backup data is transmitted to backup storage via SAN (LAN-free storage must be configured first)<br><br>Agent: Transmitted to backup storage via agent resource pool or single transport agent<br><br>If SAN transport fails, network transport will be used automatically",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_SMARTX_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>Agent: Transmitted to backup storage via agent resource pool or single transport agent",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_OPENSTACK_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network<br><br>Agent: Transmitted to backup storage via agent resource pool or single transport agent",
    'UI_BACKUP_TRANSPORT_XENSERVER_SELECT_NO_LANFREE_TIPS2' => "Network transport: Backup data will be transmitted to backup storage via LAN network",
    'UI_BACKUP_DATA_RESERVE_TYPE_TIPS' => "Retention policy of backup data ",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE' => "Advanced Backup Mode",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_TIPS' => "Advanced options to backup easier ",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_HIGH_SPEED' => "SpeedKit",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_HIGH_SPEED_TIPS' => "SpeedKit can help improving the computing speed of changed data blocks when doing incremental backups. It is recommended to be enabled if you want faster incremental backups.",
    'UI_BACKUP_KEEP_SNAPSHOT' => "Retain Snapshot",
    'UI_BACKUP_KEEP_SNAPSHOT_TIPS' => "If enabled, a snapshot will be retained for rapid recovery within the same availability zone.",
    'UI_BACKUP_SNAPSHOT_TIMEOUT' => "Snapshot Timeout",
    'UI_BACKUP_SNAPSHOT_TIMEOUT_SECOND' => "Snapshot Timeout (Seconds)",
    'UI_BACKUP_SNAPSHOT_TIMEOUT_TIPS' => "The time it takes to create a snapshot for an instance depends on the disk size. If the timeout is exceeded, snapshot creation will stop",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_TIPS' => "SpeedKit is a Vinchin technology to improve the computing speed of changed data blocks when doing incremental backups. It is recommended to be selected if you want faster incremental backups or when CBT doesn't work. (Precondition: you have sufficient production storage space.) <br><br>CBT (Changed Block Tracking) is the top recommended incremental mode to run VM incremental backups. <br><br> Ordinary mode will take more time to do incremental backups.",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_TIPS_EN' => "SpeedKit is a Vinchin technology to improve the computing speed of changed data blocks when doing incremental backups. It is recommended to be selected if you want faster incremental backups or when CBT doesn’t work. (Precondition: you have sufficient production storage space.) <br><br> Ordinary mode will take more time to do incremental backups.",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_CTB_TIPS' => "CBT (Changed Block Tracking) is the top recommended incremental mode to run VM incremental backups. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_HIGH_SPEED_CBT_TIPS' => "SpeedKit is a Vinchin technology to improve the computing speed of changed data blocks when doing incremental backups. It is recommended to be selected if you want faster incremental backups or when CBT doesn't work. (Precondition: you have sufficient production storage space.) <br><br>CBT (Changed Block Tracking) is the top recommended incremental mode to run VM incremental backups.",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_NORMAL_CBT_TIPS' => "Normal: No snapshots are retained, more time is needed before the backup job to calculate valid data.<br><br>CBT: No snapshots are retained, valid data is calculated using change block tracking technology.",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_H3CCVD_TIPS' => "Adaptive Incremental Mode will choose the following incremental modes based on the virtual machine's disk type and current snapshot status:<br><br>Standard: Does not retain any snapshots; more time is required before the backup job to compute valid data.<br><br>CBT: High-speed disks enable CBT (Change Block Tracking) during backups, retaining one support external snapshot, and use change block tracking technology to compute valid data.",
    'UI_BACKUP_INC_MODE_HYPERV_TIPS' => "High-speed: A snapshot will be retained after backup to accelerate locating valid data<br><br>Disabled: No snapshots will be retained, requiring more time to calculate valid data before backup jobs, only full backups are available",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_HIGH_SILENTSNAPSHOT' => "Quiesced Snapshot",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_HIGH_SILENTSNAPSHOT_TIPS' => "By enabling <strong>Quiesced Snapshot</strong> to keep file systems or applications on the VM in a consistent state via application-awareness processing (e.g. VMware Tools) before taking the VM snapshot.<br><br> Applications on Windows OS are required to support Microsoft VSS. <br><br> If failed to take quiesced snapshot, system will take standard snapshot. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_HIGH_HUAWEI_KVM_SILENTSNAPSHOT_TIPS' => "By enabling <strong>Consistent Snapshot</strong> to keep file systems or applications on the VM in a consistent state via application-awareness processing (e.g. VMware Tools) before taking the VM snapshot.<br><br> Applications on Windows OS are required to support Microsoft VSS. <br><br> If failed to take the consistent snapshot, system will take standard snapshot. ",
    'UI_BACKUP_MODE_HIGH_CBT_TIPS' => "Enabling <strong>CBT</strong> can improve speed of incremental backups. Supported by virtual machine version 7 or above.",
